contentText:
Once a hip-hop capital and the genre&#8217;s centrifugal force, Atlanta&#8217;s rap scene has seen a decline and become a fractured community since the sprawling YSL RICO trial.

Offset joined New York Times&#8217; Popcast on Thursday (Nov. 12), during which he explained why he stood by Gunna after the &#8220;Fukumean&#8221; rapper faced allegations of snitching once he reached an Alford plea deal in the YSL RICO case in 2022 to regain his freedom.

